  c. copy the Software for backup, archival or private use;
  d. fork the repository, modify it, and run your modified version;
  e. publish your fork or Modification — but only if you follow section 3;
  f. quote short excerpts in articles, tutorials, talks or reviews, with a
     link back to this repository;
  g. submit issues and pull requests back to this repository.


3. CONDITIONS FOR FORKS AND MODIFICATIONS
-----------------------------------------

If you fork, modify, or share the Software or a Modification with anyone, you
must:

  a. keep this license file, unchanged, in the copy;
  b. keep the original copyright notice ("Copyright (c) 2026 Maryam Mumtaz")
     in the source files and in the README;
  c. give clear, visible credit in the README and in the app's About or footer
     area, in this form:

       "Based on SketchSpace by Maryam Mumtaz —
        https://github.com/MaryamMumtaz-piaic/sketch-space"

  d. state clearly which parts you changed, and mark modified files or sections
     as modified;
  e. license your Modification under this same license, with no additional
     restrictions;
  f. keep the project name "SketchSpace" for the fork, and label it as a
     derivative work (for example: "SketchSpace — community fork"), so nobody
     mistakes it for a separate original project;
  g. if you publish your changes, tell the Author. Opening an issue or a pull
     request in this repository is the easiest way to do that. This is a
     courtesy request rather than a legal condition.


